    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Bifurcation diagrams aren&#x27;t only for discrete maps -- they&#x27;re just as useful for continuous, periodically-forced flows, via a stroboscopic Poincare section: sampling the state once per forcing period turns the continuous flow into an effective discrete map. The flow swept here is the forced, damped Duffing oscillator,">

